  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CDW Government is a federal vendor with $305M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 725 awards and an average award size of $421K. Obligations are up 11.1% year over year, following a multi-year trend that peaked at $468M in FY22 and then declined before rising this fiscal year. The Department of Transportation is the dominant buyer, accounting for $236M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Systems Design Services are the largest markets by obligation, totaling $141M and $113M respectively. Smaller but notable buying agencies include the Department of Defense with $34.4M and the Department of Agriculture with $13.5M. CDW Government sells hardware and systems through Electronic Computer Manufacturing and software and services through Computer Systems Design Services and Other Computer Related Services, which together make up the bulk of current-year obligations. The FY2026 totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date obligations rather than full year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed compared with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY26 obligations are $305M. Obligations are up 11.1% year over year compared with the prior fiscal year. Annual obligations peaked at $468M in FY22 and then fell to $274M in FY25 before the current-year increase."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets account for most FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation accounts for $236M of FY2026 obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Systems Design Services account for $141M and $113M respectively, together representing the largest markets for CDW Government this fiscal year."
      }
